ange of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Must for Personal Obligation", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use and hear the modal <span class=\"strong\">must</span> in many contexts. When you want to refer to an obligation that you put on yourself, you can use <span class=\"strong\">must</span> rather than <span class=\"strong\">have to</span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you oblige yourself to do something, it means that you impose a certain duty on yourself for some reason. When you want to communicate that idea, you can use <span class=\"strong\">must</span>. You use have to when the obligation is imposed upon you from an outside authority.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">must</span> remember to make that dentist appointment - I keep forgetting! <br/>I <span class=\"strong\">must</span> buy my sister a birthday present - her birthday is next week! <br/>We <span class=\"strong\">have to</span> wear a uniform at work. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"italic\">must</span> stay healthy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"italic\">have to</span> do more to support my community.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"italic\">must</span> get more practical work experience.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"italic\">must</span> be more social.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"italic\">must</span> work on my personal development.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "First Conditional: Modal Verbs Will, May, and Might ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the<span class=\"strong\"> first conditional</span> to talk about real or possible situations.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you use the modal verb will in the result clause, you communicate the fact that the result is quite possible or even certain.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure of the <span class=\"strong\">  first conditional </span>is usually<br />  If + present simple (If clause) and will + infinitive (result clause). <br /><br /> Remember to use a comma (,) if the If clause is at the beginning of the sentence.  <br />For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">If I don't study for the test, <span class=\"strong\">I won't pass</span>. </span> <br /> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">I won't pass </span>if I don't study for the test. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can choose to use <span class=\"strong\">may</span> or <span class=\"strong\">might</span> instead of <span class=\"strong\">will</span> when you want to talk about a result that is less certain. It is possible, but not definite.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">If it snows tomorrow, <span class=\"strong\">I may stay home or I might go to the mall</span>. I don't know yet. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In the<span class=\"strong\"> first conditional</span>, there is no difference in meaning between <span class=\"italic\">may</span> and <span class=\"italic\">might</span>. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If you become a volunteer, you may achieve many of them. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "New studies show that if you focus on something or someone else rather than on yourself, your outlook will change, which may alter some stress-producing mechanisms in the body.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you donate your time, local hospitals and community centers will be able to invest their precious resources in other areas.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you volunteer for a non-profit organization, you might learn something about how these organizations  operate.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you understand community needs, you may develop feelings of empathy and self-efficacy.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "primarily ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "mainly; mostly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Volunteering provides physical and mental rewards, primarily by reducing stress.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le13ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about moral and personal dilemmas.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "mechanism ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a process or procedure", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Focusing on others rather than yourself may alter some stress-producing mechanisms in the body. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le13ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "fate ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "destiny; what will happen in the future", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That feeling of optimism or happiness, or that you have gained control of your fate, helps make you a stronger person.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le13ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to donate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to give", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If you donate your time, local hospitals and community centers will be able to invest in other things. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le13ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "resources ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "money or other things required to do something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Local institutions have limited resources to fulfill their mission.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le13ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "non-profit organization", "type": "name"}, {"content": "similar to a private company but with the overall goal of helping people instead of making money", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: For example, if you volunteer for a non-profit organization, you might learn about the operations of government.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le13ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Research information about volunteer work. What can be done? Where can people work as volunteers? What are the advantages and any other relevant aspects of it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a 75 - 100 word e-mail to a friend giving suggestions on where they can do some volunteer work.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For each position, explain the advantages of doing this type of work.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I discuss volunteering and volunteer opportunities in my community.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read about volunteer positions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write an e-mail giving suggestions about volunteer positions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain the advantages of volunteering.", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le13ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}]}